# RISC0 Proof Verification Standards

## Context
- Applied when implementing proof verification for RISC0 v1.2.1
- Focuses on robust validation and error handling
- Ensures consistent verification patterns
- See 2001-risc0-api for high-level RISC0 integration guidelines
- See 2002-risc0-types for import standards
- See 2003-risc0-receipts for proof handling details

## Requirements
- Implement complete verification flow:
  - Verify receipt claims and digests
  - Validate seal bytes and journal contents
  - Check verifier parameters and exit codes
  - Handle both Composite and Succinct receipts
- Follow error handling standards:
  - Use specific error types for different verification failures
  - Include detailed context in error messages
  - Log verification failures with appropriate severity
  - Track verification metrics
- Validate proof components:
  - Check input digest matches expected
  - Verify journal format and contents
  - Validate seal bytes integrity
  - Ensure correct receipt type handling
- Implement security measures:
  - Prevent timing attacks in verification
  - Use constant-time comparison for digests
  - Validate all input parameters
  - Handle malformed proofs safely
- Track verification metrics:
  - Log verification attempts and results
  - Track timing for verification steps
  - Monitor failure rates and types
  - Record proof size statistics

## Examples

<example>
// Good: Complete verification flow
use risc0_zkvm::{Receipt, VerifierContext, sha::Digestible};

fn verify_proof(
    receipt: &Receipt,
    expected_input: &[u8],
) -> Result<(), VerificationError> {
    // 1. Verify receipt claim
    let claim = receipt.claim()?;
    let digest = claim.digest();
    
    // 2. Validate input digest
    let input_digest = sha::digest(expected_input);
    if !constant_time_eq(&digest, &input_digest) {
        return Err(VerificationError::InputMismatch);
    }
    
    // 3. Verify receipt based on type
    match &receipt.inner {
        InnerReceipt::Succinct(sr) => {
            verify_succinct_receipt(sr)?;
        }
        InnerReceipt::Composite(cr) => {
            verify_composite_receipt(cr)?;
        }
        _ => return Err(VerificationError::UnknownReceiptType),
    }
    
    // 4. Check exit codes
    let params = receipt.metadata.verifier_parameters;
    match params.as_bytes() {
        [0, ..] => Ok(()), // Halted normally
        [1, code, ..] => Err(VerificationError::Paused(*code)),
        [2, ..] => Err(VerificationError::SystemLimit),
        _ => Err(VerificationError::InvalidExitCode),
    }
}
</example>

<example>
// Good: Verification with metrics
fn verify_with_metrics(receipt: &Receipt) -> Result<(), VerificationError> {
    emit_event_with_duration!(MetricEvents::ProofVerification, {
        let result = verify_proof(receipt);
        if let Err(ref e) = result {
            emit_event!(MetricEvents::VerificationFailed,
                error => e.to_string(),
                receipt_type => receipt.inner.type_name()
            );
        }
        result
    }, receipt_type => receipt.inner.type_name())
}
</example>

